    "ls|LS17_S12_U_286": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILYWELFARE\nDEPARTMENTOF HEALTH AND FAMILYWELFARE\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO-286\nTO BE ANSWERED ON- 21/07/2023\nSETTING UP OF AIIMS INSTITUTES\n286. SHRI M. BADRUDDIN AJMAL:\nSHRI VISHNU DATT SHARMA:\nSHRI JANARDAN SINGH SIGRIWAL:\nADV .ADOOR PRAKASH:\nSHRI KODIKUNNIL SURESH:\nSHRI ANTO ANTONY:\nWill the Minister of HEALTHAND FAMILYWELFARE be pleased to state:-\n(a) whether the Government has been making efforts to establish All India Institutes of Medical\nSciences (AIIMS) in many States including Assam for the past several years and if so, the details\nthereof;\n(b) the number of AIIMS functional in the States/UTs other than Delhi;\n(c) the details of the under construction AIIMS for the last several years which have not been\ncompleted till date along with the reasons therefor;\n(d) whether the Government has taken stock of the status of these Branches of AIIMS; and\n(e) if so, the details thereof including current status each of such AIIMS including in Assam,\nKerala and Patna?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATEIN THE MINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILY\nWELFARE\n(DR. BHARATI PRA VINPAWAR)\n(a) to (e) Pradhan Mantri Swasthya Suraksha Yojana (PMSSY) Scheme was announced in\n2003 and was launched in 2006. The scheme aims at correcting regional imbalances in the\navailability of affordable tertiary healthcare services and augmenting facilities for quality\nmedical education in the country.Under the Scheme, setting up of 22 new AIIMS have been\n\napproved by the Cabinet in various phases. Status of functionality of all 22 new AIIMS including\nin Assam and Patna is at Annexure.\nThe Ministry closely and regularly monitors the progress of new AIIMS projects with all\nstakeholders to facilitate speedy completion of the projects. Completion of works depends upon\nvarious factors including transfer of encumbrance free land by the State Government, regulatory\nclearances and site specific issues.\n\nAnnexure\nDETAILS OF 22 AIIMS INSTITUTES UNDER PMSSY\nS. No. Phase\nLocation of\nAIIMS under\nPMSSY\nDate of\nCabinet\nApproval\nStatus of Functionality\n1 to 6 Six (06) AIIMS at Bhopal (Madhya Pradesh), Bhubaneswar (Odisha), Jodhpur\n(Rajasthan), Patna (Bihar), Raipur (Chhattisgarh) and Rishikesh (Uttarakhand)\nestablished under Phase I of PMSSY ,are fully functional\n7 Phase-II\nAIIMS, Raebareli 05.02.2009  Construction completed\n MBBS classes commenced\nfrom academic year 2019-20\n OPD services operationalised\n Limited IPD functional\n8\nPhase-IV\nMangalagiri in\nAndhra Pradesh\n07.10.2015  Construction completed\n MBBS classes commenced\nfrom academic year 2018-19\n OPD services\noperationalised\n Limited IPD functional\n9\nNagpur in\nMaharashtra\n07.10.2015  Construction completed\n MBBS classes commenced\nfrom academic year 2018-\n19.\n OPD services operationalised.\n Limited IPD functional.\n10\nKalyani in\nWest Bengal\n07.10.2015  Construction completed\n MBBS classes commenced\nfrom academic year 2019-20.\n OPD services\noperationalised.\n Limited IPD functional\n\nS. No. Phase\nLocation of\nAIIMS under\nPMSSY\nDate of\nCabinet\nApproval\nStatus of Functionality\n11\nGorakhpur in Uttar\nPradesh\n20.07.2016  Construction completed\n MBBS classes commenced\nfrom academic year 2019-20.\n OPD services\noperationalised.\n Limited IPD functional\n12\nPhase-V\nBathinda in Punjab 27.07.2016  Construction completed\n MBBS classes commenced\nfrom academic year 2019-20.\n OPD services\noperationalised.\n Limited IPD functional\n13\nGuwahati in\nAssam\n24.05.2017  90% Construction has been\ncompleted\n MBBS classes commenced\nfrom academic year 2020-21\nfrom a temporary campus\n OPD services\noperationalised.\n Limited IPD functional\n14 Bilaspur in\nHimachal Pradesh\n03.01.2018  Construction completed\n MBBS classes commenced\nfrom academic year 2020-21.\n OPD services operationalised.\n Limited IPD functional\n15 Madurai in Tamil\nNadu\n17.12.2018  Pre-investment work\ncompleted.\n Loan Agreement signed with\nJICA on 26.03.2021\n Project Management\nConsultant appointed.\n MBBS classes commenced\nfrom academic year 2021-22\nfrom a temporary campus.\n16 Darbhanga in\nBihar\n15.09.2020 Encumbrance free land has not\nbeen handed over by the State\nGovt.\n\nS. No. Phase\nLocation of\nAIIMS under\nPMSSY\nDate of\nCabinet\nApproval\nStatus of Functionality\n17 Vijaypur in Jammu 10.01.2019  79% Construction has been\ncompleted\n MBBS classes commenced\nfrom academic year 2020-21\nfrom a temporary campus\n18 Awantipora in\nKashmir\n10.01.2019  32% Construction has been\ncompleted\n19\nPhase-VI\nDeoghar in\nJharkhand\n16.05.2018  95% Construction has been\ncompleted\n MBBS classes commenced\nfrom academic year 2019-20\nfrom a temporary campus.\n OPD services operationalised.\n Limited IPD functional\n20 Rajkot in Gujarat 10.01.2019  60% Construction has been\ncompleted\n MBBS classes commenced\nfrom academic year 2020-21\nfrom a temporary campus.\n OPD services operationalised.\n21 Bibinagar in\nTelangana\n17.12.2018  21% Construction has been\ncompleted\n MBBS classes commenced\nfrom academic year 2019-20.\n OPD services operationalised.\n Limited IPD functional\n22 Phase-VII Manethi in\nHaryana\n28.02.2019  State Government has\nidentified alternate land at\nvillage Majra in Rewari\ndistrict for AIIMS project.\n Lease deed executed for 200\nAcres of land\n Agency for pre-investment\nactivities and main work\nappointed.\n Pre-investment work started.\n*****",
    "ls|LS17_S12_U_287": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF AYUSH\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.287\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21.07.2023\nSCHEME FOR DEVELOPMENT OF AYUSH ENTREPRENEURSHIP\n287. SHRI SUNIL BABURAO MENDHE:\nWill the Minister of Ayush be pleased to state:\n(a) whether any scheme for the development of AYUSH entrepreneurship is being chalked out to\npromote AYUSH sector in the country, State/UT-wise particularly in Maharashtra;\n(b) if so, the details thereof;\n(c) whether the Government has formulated any proposal to include youth and scientists in\nnation building opportunities in various sectors of AYUSH like research, innovation,\nmanagement, medical, higher education etc.; and\n(d) if so, the details thereof?”\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF AYUSH\n(SHRI SARBANANDA SONOWAL)\n(a) & (b)\nFor the purpose of development of the Ayush entrepreneurship Ministry of Ayush had developed\na Central Sector Scheme namely Champion Services Sector Scheme for Medical Value Travel\nfor implementation on Pan India basis. Under this scheme, financial assistance in the form of\nInterest Subsidy is provided to private investors for the establishment of Super Specialty\nHospitals/ Day Care Centres of the systems recognized under Indian Medicine Central Council\n(IMCC) Act, 1970 or Homeopathic Central Council (HCC) Act, 1973.\nMinistry of Ayush signed a MoU with Ministry of Micro, Small & Medium Enterprises (MSME)\nfor the promotion of Ayush enterprises. In this regard, 10 Awareness programmes on Digital\nAdvertisement, E-Marketing, GST& GeM were organized and 07 National Seminar / Workshop\non Packaging, Marketing and Export Promotion of Ayush Products were organized by the Micro,\nSmall & Medium Enterprises (MSME).\nThe All India Institute of Ayurveda(AIIA) an autonomous body under Ministry of Ayushhas set up\nan incubation centre i.e. AIIA-ICAINE (Incubation Centre for Ayurveda Innovation and\nEntrepreneurship) to support new startups in theAyushsector.\n\nAlso, Academia-industry Research Incubation for Value-chain Up-gradation(ARIVU) was setup\nby Central Council of Research in Siddha (CCRS) to promote innovation and entrepreneurship by\ntranslating novel ideas and innovation in various disciplines of Siddha Research, into products,\nprocesses and services for commercial exploitation and the benefit of society.\n(c) & (d)\nMinistry of Ayush has collaborated with scientific Organizations like Council of Scientific and\nIndustrial Research (CSIR), Indian Council of Agricultural Research (ICAR), Department of\nBiotechnology (DBT),Department of Science and Technology (DST) and Indian Council of\nMedical Research (ICMR) to promote research, innovation, management and higher education\netc.\nThe Central Council for Research in Ayurvedic Sciences (CCRAS) has initiated “CCRAS Post\nDoctoral Fellowship Scheme” with the approval of Ministry of Ayush to offer ten (10) such\nfellowships every year to promising fresh PhD/PG degree holders of Ayurveda and Ph.D. holders.\nThe scheme has been instituted for identifying promising young researchers with innovative\nideas and provides them with training and research opportunities in Ayurveda and other allied\nsciences.\nThe Scheme for Training in Ayurveda Research for PG Scholars (PG-STAR) has been launched\non 14-06-2023 for Ayurveda Post Graduate Scholars pursuing their MD/MS(Ayu) courses. This\nscheme is primarily aimed at promoting good quality research in Ayurveda students pursuing\npost-graduation courses as well as to improve visibility and accessibility of their research work\nto larger research audience.\nThe Studentship Program for Ayurveda Research KEN (SPARK) has been launched in 02-09-\n2022 in order to promote interest and aptitude for research among Ayurveda undergraduates. The\nmain objective of this program is to provide an opportunity to undergraduate Ayurveda students\nto familiarize themselves with Research Methodology and techniques.\nAlso, a MoU was signed by Central Council of Research in Siddha (CCRS) on 06-11-2019 with\nAccelerating Growth of New India Innovation (AGNIi) for the commercialization of R&D\ntechnologies and products development.\n******",
    "ls|LS17_S12_U_288": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO-288\nANSWERED ON- 21/07/2023\nPASSPORT SEVA KENDRAS\n†288.  DR. DHAL SINGH BISEN\n     SHRI SUNIL BABURAO MENDHE\n     SHRI ARUN KUMAR SAGAR\n     DR. ALOK KUMAR SUMAN\nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state :-\n(a)  the  number  of passport  offices/Passport  Service  Kendras (PSKs)  functioning in the\ncountry, State/UT-wise including Madhya Pradesh, Bihar and Maharashtra;\n(b) the number of applications received for issuing passport in each passports offices/service\nkendras and the number of passports issued/renewed during the last three years at these\ncentres, State-wise including Madhya Pradesh, Bihar and Gondia district of Maharashtra;\n(c) whether the Government has any proposal to open more Passport Centres in the country\nto meet the rising demand for passports and if so, the details\n(d) the criteria fixed for the setting up of new Regional Passport Offices in the country;\n(e)  the  details  of  the  schemes formulated  for  the  modernisation  and  expansion  of  the\npassport offices in the country at present;\n(f) whether there is any shortage of manpower and infrastructure facilities at these centres\nand if so, the details thereof, State-wise including Madhya Pradesh and Bihar; and\n(g) the remedial measures taken by the Government in this regard?\nANSWER\n       THE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS\n       (SHRI V. MURALEEDHARAN)\n(a) As on date there are 36 Passport Offices under whom 93 Passport Service Kendras\n(PSKs)  and  430  Post  Office  Passport  Seva  Kendras  (POPSKs)  are  functioning  in  the\ncountry including Madhya Pradesh, Bihar and Maharashtra. List is attached at Annexure-I\n& II.  \n(b)  The  number  of  applications  received  for  issuing  passport  in  each  passports\noffices/service kendras and the number of passports issued/renewed during the last three\nyears at these centres, State-wise including Madhya Pradesh, Bihar and Gondia district of\nMaharashtra is attached as Annexure-III.\n(c) Ministry in association with Department of Posts (DoP) had announced in the year 2017,\nthe opening of Passport Kendras at the Head Post Offices (HPO)/ Post Offices  (PO)  in  the\ncountry called Post Office Passport Seva Kendra (POPSK) in each Lok Sabha Constituency\n1\n\nwhere there is no Passport Seva Kendra (PSK). As on date, there are 430 Post Office\nPassport Seva Kendras have been established and are functional in the country to meet the\nrising demand for passport. Details of PSKs and POPSKs is attached at Annexure-I & II.\n(d) The opening of new Regional Passport Office in the country depends on various factors,\nincluding distance from the existing Passport Kendras and volume of applications from a\nparticular region, as well as other relevant factors.\n(e) All the Passport Offices, the PSKs and the POPSKs in the country are fully modernised.\nAfter the nation-wide roll-out of the Passport Seva Programme, the Passport Offices, the\nPSKs and POPSKs are supported by state-of-the-art technology and infrastructure which\nenables end-to-end passport services to be delivered with enhanced security.  The Passport\nSeva  Programme  Version  2.0  (PSP  V2.0)  aims  at  providing  the  next  level  of  citizen\nexperiences using latest and upgraded technology for delivery of passport related services to\nthe citizens in a speedy, convenient and transparent manner. \n(f & g) As the recruitment is made through Staff Selection Commission (SSC), it endeavours\nto fill the vacancies soon. There is shortage of manpower in many Regional Passport Offices\n(RPOs) in the country including State of Madhya Pradesh, Bihar and Maharashtra.\nMeanwhile, Ministry has hired 7, 10 and 55 Data Entry Operators (DEOs) and Multi Tasking\nStaffs (MTSs) from Outsourced Agency in Passport Offices located in the states of Madhya\nPradesh, Bihar and Maharashtra, respectively as an interim measure for smooth functioning\nof the Passport Offices.\n                                                                                *****\n2\n\nAnnexure-I\nS.NO RPO Name PSK S.NO PSK Name\n1 RPO Ahmedabad 1 PSK Mithakali Ahmedabad\n2 PSK Rajkot\n3 PSK Vadodara\n4 PSK Vijay Cross Road Ahmedabad\n2 RPO Amritsar 5 PSK Amritsar\n3 RPO Bareilly 6 PSK Bareilly\n4 RPO Bengaluru 7 PSK Bengaluru, Lalbagh\n8 PSK Bengaluru, Sai Arcade\n9 PSK Hubballi-Dharwad\n10 PSK Mangaluru\n11 PSLK Kalaburagi\n5 RPO Bhopal 12 PSK Bhopal\n13 PSLK Indore\n6 RPO Bhubaneswar 14 PSK Bhubaneswar\n7 RPO Chandigarh 15 PSK Ambala\n16 PSK Chandigarh\n17 PSK Ludhiana\n8 RPO Chennai 18 PSK Aminjikarai\n19 PSK Saligramam\n20 PSK Tambaram\n21 PSLK Puducherry\n9 RPO Cochin 22 PSK Alappuzha\n23 PSK Aluva\n24 PSK Kottayam\n25 PSK Thrissur\n26 PSK Tripunithura, Cochin\n10 RPO Coimbatore 27 PSK Coimbatore\n11 RPO Dehradun 28 PSK Dehradun\n12 RPO Delhi 29 PSK R.K Puram\n30 PSK Gurgaon\n31 PSK Herald House - ITO\n32 PSK Shalimar Place\n13 RPO Ghaziabad 33 PSK Ghaziabad\n14 RPO Guwahati 35 PSK Guwahati\n36 PSLK Aizawl\n3\n\n37 PSLK Dimapur\n38 PSLK Imphal\n39 PSLK Itanagar\n40 PSLK Shillong\n15 RPO Hyderabad 41 PSK Ameerpet\n42 PSK Begumpet\n43 PSK Nizamabad\n44 PSK Toli Chowki\n45 PSLK Karimnagar\n16 RPO Jaipur 46 PSK Jaipur\n47 PSK Jodhpur\n48 PSK Sikar\n49 PSLK Udaipur\n17 RPO Jalandhar 50 PSK Hoshiarpur\n51 PSK Jalandhar-1\n52 PSK Jalandhar-2\n18 RPO Jammu 53 PSK Jammu\n19 RPO Kolkata 54 PSK Berhampore\n55 PSK Kolkata\n56 PSLK Agartala\n57 PSLK Gangtok\n58 PSLK Siliguri\n20 RPO Kozhikode 59 PSK Kannur\n60 PSK Kozhikode\n61 PSK Malappuram II\n62 PSK Payyanur, Kannur\n63 PSK Vadakara, Kozhikode\n21\nRPO Lucknow 64 PSK Gorakhpur\n65 PSK Kanpur\n66 PSK Lucknow\n67 PSK Varanasi\n22 RPO Madurai 68 PSK Madurai\n69 PSK Tirunelveli City\n23 RPO Mumbai 70 PSK Andheri\n71 PSK Lower Parel\n72 PSK Malad\n73 PSK Nashik II\n4\n\n74 PSK Thane II\n24 RPO Nagpur 75 PSK Nagpur\n25 RPO Panaji 34 PSK Panaji\n26 