    "ls|LS17_S12_U_362": "1\nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF AYUSH\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.362\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21ST JULY,2023\nAYURVEDICHOSPITALS IN HARYANA\n†362. SHRI NAYABSINGH:\nWill the Minister of AYUSH be pleased to state:\n(a) the number of Ayurvedic hospitals functioning in the country particularly in Haryana and\nKurukshetra Parliamentary Constituency;\n(b) if so, the details thereof, State/UT-wise;\n(c) whether the Government has any plan to set up AYUSH Hospitals in each district of the\ncountry particularly in Haryana and Kurukshetra Parliamentary Constituency;\n(d) if so, the details thereof, State/UT-wise; and\n(e) the measures taken/proposed to be taken by the Government to set up more AYUSH\nHospitals in the country?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF AYUSH\n(SHRI SARBANANDA SONOWAL)\n(a) & (b) The number of Ayurvedic Hospitals functioning State/UT-wise in the country including\nHaryana is furnished at Annexure-I. Further, 1 (one) Ayurvedic hospital is functioning in\nKurukshetra district.\n(c) to (e) Public Health being a State subject, setting up of Ayush Hospitals in any district of any\nState/UT, comes under the purview of respective State/UT Governments. However, under\nCentrally Sponsored Scheme of National Ayush Mission (NAM), there is a provision of financial\nassistance to States/UTs for setting up of 50/30/10 bedded integrated Ayush hospitals.\nAccordingly, State/UT Governments including Haryana may avail financial assistance by\nsubmitting suitable proposal through State Annual Action Plan (SAAP) as per the provision of\nNAM guideline. Further, as per the proposals received from the State/UT Governments including\nHaryana, the status of approved integrated Ayush Hospitals for setting up in the country is\nfurnished as Annexure-II.\n\n2\nAnnexure-I\nThe number of Ayurvedic Hospitals functioning State/UT-wise (as on 01.04.2021)\nS. No. State / UT No. of Ayurvedic Hospitals\n1 Andhra Pradesh 3\n2 Arunachal Pradesh 10\n3 Assam 1\n4 Bihar 