    "ls|LS17_S12_U_387": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF WOMEN AND CHILD DEVELOPMENT \n  \nLOK SABHA \n UN-STARRED QUESTION NO. 387 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21.07.2023 \n  \nONE STOP CENTRES IN ANDHRA PRADESH \n  \n387.   SHRI MAGUNTA SREENIVASULU REDDY:  \n \nWill the Minister of Women and Child Development be pleased to state: \n  \n(a) the details of the One Stop Centres currently operational in the State of Andhra \nPradesh, districtwise;  \n(b) the details of funds allocated towards such centres during the last three years, \nyear-wise; and  \n(c) the details of services provided to women in the said centres?  \n  \n  \nANSWER \n  \nMINISTER OF WOMEN AND CHILD DEVELOPMENT \n(SHRIMATI SMRITI ZUBIN IRANI) \n  \n  \n(a) & (b): The One Stop Centre (OSC) scheme implemented by the Government since \n1st April, 2015 is now a component of sub -scheme 'Sambal' under umbrella scheme \nfor safety, security and empowerment of women named 'Mission Shakti'. So far, a total \nof 26 One Stop Centres have been approved for 26 Districts of Andhra Pradesh, out \nof which 13  OSCs are functional. The district -wise details of functional OSCs and \nfunds released to these centres during the last three years are at Annexure-I.  \n  \n(c): OSCs are set up with the objective to provide a range of integrated services under \none roof includ ing police facilitation, medical aid, legal aid and legal counselling, \npsycho-social counselling and temporary shelter to women affected by violence or \ndistress. \n  \n**** \n  \n\nANNEXURE-I \n  \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) & (b) OF THE LOK SABHA \nUN-STARRED QUESTION NO.387 FOR 21.07.2023 ASKED BY SHRI MAGUNTA \nSREENIVASULU REDDY REGARDING ‘ONE STOP CENTRES IN ANDHRA \nPRADESH’  \n  \nDistrict wise details of functional and non -functional OSCs and funds released \nto these centres during the last three years : \nSl. \nNo. \nDistricts Function \nStatus \n2020-21 2021-22 2022-23 \n1 Ananthapuram Yes 1500450 1500450 0 \n2 Chittoor-A Yes 1250375 1500450 0 \n3 Kakinda formerly East Godavari Yes 1850375 1500450 0 \n4 Guntur Yes 1500450 1500450 0 \n5 Dr. YSR Kadapa Yes 1250375 1500450 0 \n6 Kurnool Yes 1850375 1500450 0 \n7 SPSR Nellore Yes 1250375 1500450 0 \n8 Prakasm Yes 1850375 3325450 1326739 \n9 Srikakulam Yes 2100450 1500450 0 \n10 NTR formerly Krishna Yes 1850375 1500450 2385588 \n11 Visakhapatnam Yes 1500450 1500450 2813774 \n12 Vizianagaram Yes 1500450 1500450 769554 \n13 Eluru formerly West Godavari Yes 1250375 1500450 0 \n14 Tirupathi formerly Chittor-B* No 0 3625911* 0 \nTotal 20505250 24956761 7295655 \n*Funds released for recurring expenditure and construction activities. \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S12_U_388": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO-388\nANSWERED ON- 21/07/2023\nINDIAN COMMUNITY WELFARE FUND \n 388. ADV . A.M. ARIFF\nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state :-\n(a) the details of balance amount available in Indian Community Welfare Fund (ICWF) in each of\nthe Indian Embassy/High Commission abroad as on 30.06.2023, country-wise;\n(b) whether the Government has utilised the amount available with ICWF for helping Indians\ninvolved  in  legal  disputes  during  the  Financial  Year  2019-23,  if  so,  the  details  thereof,\nEmbassy/High Commission-wise; and\n(c) whether the Government has utilized the amount available with ICWF for bringing back the\nmortal remains of Indians who had expired during their stay abroad during the said period and if so,\nthe details thereof?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS\n(SHRI V . MURALEEDHARAN)\n(a) The details of balance amount available in Indian Community Welfare Fund (ICWF) in each of\nthe  Indian  Embassy/High  Commission  abroad  as  on  30.06.2023,  country-wise  is  given  in\nAnnexure I.\n(b & c) Missions / Posts abroad are authorized to incur expenditure on different welfare activities\non  actual  need  basis  within  prescribed  ceilings.  Expenditure  beyond  prescribed  ceilings  on  a\nparticular welfare activity can also be incurred, if required, with prior approval of the Ministry. The\nMission wise details of expenditure incurred from Indian Community Welfare Fund (ICWF)  from\n2019 till June 2023, for providing legal assistance to  Indian nationals and expenditure incurred on\ntransportation of mortal remains from the country of death to India are given in Annexure II.\n*****\n1\n\nAnnexure – I\nSl. No. Name of the country\nAvailable balance in ICWF as on \n30.06.2023\n1 Algeria  21,15,838.00₹\n2 Angola  16,33,922.00₹\n3 Argentina  2,33,248.00₹\n4 Armenia  12,88,712.00₹\n5 Australia  27