    "ls|LS17_S12_U_395": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF PORTS, SHIPPING AND WATERWAYS\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 395\nANSWERED ON 21 .O7.2023\nIMPORTS AND EXPORTS THROUGH PORTS\n395. SHRI NIHAL CHAND:\nwiil the Minister of PoRTS, SHIPPING AND WATERWAYS be pleased to state:\nqt-{. frdqftTrr eiltre+P165\n(a) the number of ports in the country at present, State/UT-wise;\n(b) the quantum of imports and exports made through these ports during the last two\nyears;\n(c) the number of ports out of these which have been developed with modern facilities\nalong with the details of facilities available therein;\n(d) the details of the future development plans of these ports;\n(e) whether the Government is contemplating to set up new ports and if so, the details\nthereof; and\n(f) the number of ports constructed/developed in the country since the inception of\nSagarmala Project scheme, State/UT-wise?\nANSWER\nMINISTER OF PORTS, SHIPPING AND WATERWAYS\n(SHRI SARBANANDA SONOWAL)\n(a) The details of total functional Major and Ports other than Major Ports (Non-\nMaior Ports), State/UT-wise are at Annexure l'\n(b) The volume of import and export carried out through Major and Ports other than\nMajor Ports (Non Major Ports) during the last two years is at Annexure ll'\n(c)to(0TheMajorPortsoflndiaareregulatedunderMa,;orPortsAuthorityAct,\n202l.However,PortsotherthanMalorPorts(Non-MajorPorts)andtheir\nconcessionaires are regulated by Sate Maritime Boards under respective State\nGovernments. Under sagarmala Programme, Ministry provides financial assistance\nto state government port infrastructure pro.iects, coastal berth projects, road and rail\nprojects, fishery harbours, skill development projects' Coastal Community\nDevelopment'cruiseterminalandpro'iectssuchasRo-Paxferryservicesetc'Under\n\n-z*\nthe port modernization pillar of sagarmala Programme, 19 projects worth Rs. 1,180\ncr. have been financially supported through sagarmala scheme. out of which, 6\nprojects worth Rs. 220 Cr. have been completed.\nThe state wise break up of overall Sagarmala funded projects is annexed'\n[Annexure-lll]\nGovernment of lndia has accorded approval for development of Major Port at\nVadhavan in Maharashtra on landlord Port development model due to its natural\nadvantages and growing requirement of lmport export trade of country. Galathea Bay\nin Great Nicobar lsland of Andaman & Nicobar lslands has also been identified for\ndevelopment of an lnternational Container Transhipment Terminal due to its strategic\nlocation.\n\n4-\nAnnexure I\nState / UT No of\nPorts Other than Major\nPorts (Non Maior Ports)\nNo of\nMajor ports\nAndhra Pradesh 15 1\nGoa 5 1\nGuja rat 4B 1\nKarnataka 13 1\nKerala 17 1\nMaharashtra 48 2\nOdisha 14 1\nTamil Nadu 17 a\nWest Bengal 1 1\nAndaman and Nicobar\nlslands 24\nDaman & Diu 2\nPuducherry a\nLakshadweep 10\n\n- L{-\n(P): Provisional\n(b) Overseas and Coastal Cargo at Non-Major Ports of State Maritime Board/ Directorate of\nPorts during 2020-21, 2021-22 (Pl (in Million tonnes)\nAnnexure-ll\nOverseas and Coastal Carqo at Maior Ports duting 2021-22' 2022-23 Million tonnes\nStates PORT/ YEAR\n2021-22 2022-23(P\\\nOverseas Coastal Total Overseas Coastal Total\nGuiarat DEENDAYAL 111.08 16.02 127.10 123 88 13.68 137.56\nl\\4aharashtra\nMumbai 35.79 24 10 59.89 41.00 llot 63.61\nJ,L NEHRU 71 88 412 76.00 78.97 4.90 83.87\nGoa MORMUGAO 16 34 211 18 46 15.64 1.68 17.32\nKarnataka NEW MANGALORE 29.40 9.89 39 30 31.96 9.47 41 42\nKerala COCH IN 22 71 11 84 34 55 23.15 12.11 35.26\nTamil Nadu\nv.o.\nCH IDAMBARANAR 23.56 10.56 34.12 25 27 12.77 38 04\nCHENNAI 41.39 7.17 48.56 43 03 592 48 95\nKamarajar 22.50 16.24 38.74 25.81 17.69 43.51\nAnd hra Pradesh\nVISAKHAPATNAM 47.76 21 .27 69.03 54.84 18.91 73.75\nOdisha PARADIP 73.93 42.20 1 16.1 3 77.28 58.08 135.36\nWest Benqal\nSMP\n(KOLKATfuHALDIA) 52.37 5.80 58.18 59.21 5.78 64.99\nALL PORTS s48.73 171.32 720.05 600.03 183.60 783.63\nState Maritime Board/\nDirectorate of States\n202',t-22 20