    "ls|LS17_S12_U_443": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF DEFENCE \nDEPARTMENT OF DEFENCE PRODUCTION \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 443 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21st July, 2023 \nORDNANCE FACTORY \n443. SHRI NABA KUMAR SARANIA: \nWill the Minister of DEFENCE be pleased to state: \n(a)  the details of the Ordnance factories established/existing in the country, State/UT-wise; \n(b)  whether there is any proposal to increase the capacity of Ordnance factories and if so, the \ndetails thereof; \n(c)  whether there is any proposal to privatize Jabalpur Ordnance factory and if so, the details \nthereof along with the reasons behind the same; \n(d)  the total number of employees working in Ordnance factories across the country; and \n(e)  the proposal of the Government to secure the future of these employees in case of \nprivatisation of Jabalpur Ordnance factory? \n \nA  N  S  W  E  R \n \n      MINISTER OF STATE     (SHRI AJAY BHATT) \n      IN THE MINISTRY OF DEFENCE \n \n(a):  Details of Ordnance factories established/existing in the country, State/UT-wise is \nattached as Annexure: \n(b):  Yes, Sir. Ordnance Factories under the new DPSUs continuously enhance/upgrade their \ncapacity by establishing new Plant and Machineries as per the futuristic requirements of \nDefence Stores. \n(c):  No, Sir. \n(d):  As on 01.07.2023, a total of 66,429 numbers of employees are working in 41 Ordnance \nfactories, under the 07 newly created DPSUs, across the country. \n(e):  Does not arise in view of reply to part (c). \n \n***** \n \n \n \n\nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 443 TO BE ANSWERED ON 21.07.2023 \nREGARDING “ORDNANCE FACTORY”. \nSl. \nNo. \nStates/UTs Sl. \nNo. \nOrdnance Factory/UNIT \n \n \n \n \n1 \n \n \n \n \nMaharashtra \n1. Ammunition Factory Khadki \n(A unit of Munition India Limited) \n2. High Explosive Factory, Khadki \n(A unit of Munition India Limited) \n3. Ordnance Factory Bhandara \n(A unit of Munition India 